---
/**
 * The dropdown marker on the "When do you need this?" control — Figma `33:536`.
 *
 * A filled triangle, not a stroked chevron, so `Icon.astro` has no matching
 * glyph. The path is the exact geometry of the exported asset
 * (12.1244 x 10.5, fill #D9D9D9), written point-down: Figma draws the polygon
 * point-up and rotates the wrapper 180deg, which is the same shape.
 *
 * Inlined rather than committed as a file because the vector is three points
 * and the exported SVG is 266 bytes — an <img> would cost a request and could
 * not be sized against the token system.
 *
 * ⚠ It positions itself. Astro scopes CSS per component, so a `.c-arrow` rule
 * written in ContactForm.astro compiles to a selector carrying that file's
 * scope id and never matches this element; the first build of this component
 * took the class as a prop and silently laid the arrow out in flow, pushing
 * the textarea and submit 10.5px down. The offsets below are measured from the
 * enclosing `.c-select-wrap`, which is the control's own 443 x 35 box.
 */
---

<svg
  class="arrow"
  viewBox="0 0 12.1244 10.5"
  width="12.1244"
  height="10.5"
  fill="#D9D9D9"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  <path d="M0 0H12.1244L6.06218 10.5Z"></path>
</svg>

<style>
  /* Right edge at x=1332.11 (9.89px in from the control's right edge at 1342),
     top at y=530.5 (14.5px down from the control's top at 516). Both axes are
     sized explicitly: `height: auto` in global.css applies to <img>, not to an
     inline <svg>, so a width-only rule would leave the intrinsic height
     reserving a much taller box. */
  .arrow {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0.618rem;
    top: 0.90625rem;
    width: 0.7578rem;
    height: 0.65625rem;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>
